<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parthian Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Parthians, Parthian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Parthian Empire, ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsacid-dynasty">Arsacid dynasty</a>, was an Iranian state that emerged around 247 BCE and came to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. It replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> in the east and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s main rival, while controlling trade along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>. It was overthrown in 224 CE by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardashir-i">Ardashir I</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parthian-empire.jpg" alt="Parthian Empire" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original file by Ro4444, edited by me · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Parthian_Empire_under_Mithridates_II.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
